      "last_decision": {
        "at": "2026-10-19T19:32:43.615320+00:00",
        "symbol": "AAPL",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Stay flat into the 2026-10-30 FQ4 print and 2026-10-28 'Pro and Tell' event. No position is owned and the prior approved holds earlier today remain correct: the three open tests are unchanged. (1) The Q3 FY26 exhibit confirms the ~2pt tariff-refund gross-margin benefit and $0.11 of the $2.02 EPS, so Q4 organic ex-refund margin against the memory-cost headwind and the doubled inventory base ($11.1B vs $5.7B) is still unverified pending the 10-K. (2) iPhone Duo demand depth versus the 10-Q-documented DRAM/NAND supply constraint remains unresolved — the 'sold out in minutes' and delivery-pushout items are publisher claims, mutually contested by an unverified Jefferies order-cut narrative against a JPMorgan overweight, and none is primary evidence. (3) The prior packet's $55.1B other non-current liabilities decomposition remains open. This cycle's fresh broker quote (bid 342.82, between 344.51 and 341.52 earlier today) resolves only pricing, not the fundamental objections. Dated technicals confirm the intact uptrend (RSI14 62.1, MACD positive, close above SMA20/50/200) but also the ~17% extension above the 200-day at a reported ~39x P/E against a 5.1% 10Y with 2.78% real yield — duration, not credit, is the risk channel. Entering a negatively-carrying share CFD (swap_long -5.98, seven daily-equivalent debits) days before two binary events would express an unverified bullish assumption. Disclosure: full-document filing certification is unimplemented this cycle; per the owner's demo authorization this is a disclosed limitation, not an automatic veto, but it reinforces patience.",
        "thesis": "Conditional-watch thesis, no entry: the trend is intact (2026-10-16 close 343.46, RSI14 62.1, MACD positive, above SMA20/50/200, 20-session volatility 16.3% annualized, VIX 19.99 — not stressed) and filing-verified fundamentals are strong ex-one-off (Q3 FY26 revenue $109.4B +16.4%, diluted EPS $2.02 including a filing-confirmed $0.11 tariff-refund benefit and ~2pts gross margin from refunds, nine-month revenue +16%, operating income +21.7%, OCF $117B, falling debt). But the ~28% re-rating over 120 sessions embeds flawless ex-refund execution. The MD&A confirms new Section 301 tariffs and the open Section 232 semiconductor investigation as live FY27 cost risks, and the 10-Q risk factors document single-source component exposure with intensifying memory/NAND supply constraints. Entry activates only when the Oct 30 print verifies ex-refund organic margin, primary evidence separates Duo demand depth from the documented supply constraint, and the liability line decomposes benignly.",
        "countercase": "The wait is not free: if the Oct 28 event confirms Duo sell-through with delivery pushouts and the Oct 30 print shows ex-refund gross margin still expanding with an inventory drawdown, the backlog smooths FY27 revenue recognition, converts the inventory build into fulfilled upside, and entry costs 5-8% more from the current ~342.8 area. Verified name-specific relative strength (AAPL +2.2%/20 sessions vs QQQ -1.5%, IWM -4.8%) with a 1.56x-volume up session reads as accumulation, not distribution; the 10/16 close sat mid-range near the upper Bollinger band, consistent with launch repositioning. ~22% underlying EPS growth, $117B nine-month OCF and continued buybacks (shares -2.6% YoY) historically defend 30x+ multiples, and a Fed path compressing the long end would remove the main multiple risk. Refunds could also recur if tariff policy shifts. A confirmed-demand print would invalidate the de-rating risk that anchors this hold.",
        "invalidation": "This hold converts to a buy evaluation when specific source-backed evidence shows: (1) the Oct 30 FQ4 report demonstrates ex-refund organic revenue and gross-margin strength with benign refund-recurrence language in the new filings; (2) Apple-store ship dates or primary company statements confirm iPhone Duo demand depth rather than the filing-documented DRAM/NAND supply constraint; (3) the notes decompose the elevated other non-current liabilities line benignly rather than material accruals or legal exposure; and (4) price holds above the rising 20-day average through the print. It converts to a decisive avoid posture if Q4 shows refund roll-off against inventory write-down risk, the liability line contains material accruals, or price loses the 20-day and 50-day averages on widening breadth deterioration.",
        "status": "approved",
